    "gitCommitHash": "76cd555551609afefb0feb70c79919c823901b81",
    "gitCommitMessage": "scanner: bring capture back to parity with legacy Scanified\n\nCompared src\\scanner.tsx against the legacy apps Evan says worked great\n(scanified\\gas-cylinder-android + \\gas-cylinder-mobile, components\\ScanArea.tsx).\nThe autofocus constants, the 13 symbologies and the deferred-mount delay are\nalready byte-identical. The regression is everything AROUND the focus code.\n\n1. A tap on the preview now only refocuses. It used to schedule a full\n   takePictureAsync 380ms later, so the driver's reflex when a picture looks\n   soft stalled the live camera session for a full-res capture plus up to\n   five decode passes - one of them asm.js zxing on Hermes. Legacy's tap\n   toggled focus for 180ms and nothing else (ScanArea.tsx:360-369), and\n   legacy explicitly BANNED a competing capture during Locate because \"it can\n   interfere with rapid consecutive scans by competing for camera processing\"\n   (EnhancedScanScreen.tsx:2431). We had reintroduced exactly that.\n\n2. animateShutter={false} - legacy set it (ScanArea.tsx:406). The default\n   true flashes the preview white on every capture.\n\n3. shutterSound: false on both captures, as legacy did\n   (gas-cylinder-mobile ScanArea.tsx:520).\n\n4. The double-read confirm window 450ms -> 1200ms. The autofocus cycle drops\n   the lens 180ms every second BY DESIGN, so a share of frames are soft.\n   Legacy accepted on ONE good frame with a 175ms hold that only upgraded to\n   a longer candidate (ScanArea.tsx:181-254); we demanded two byte-identical\n   reads inside 450ms, which one focus hunt is enough to break. Same focus\n   code, much worse outcome, and it presents as \"the autofocus never lands.\"\n   A misread still needs a partner, so the protection is intact.\n\n5. Same-code cooldown 2500 -> 2000ms, matching legacy's own same-code dedupe\n   (EnhancedScanScreen.tsx:2404-2412).\n\nDeliberately NOT changed: the reticle height. A subagent flagged 0.28 as\nlarger than legacy's ~0.18, but reticle.ts records that 0.20 was retired\nafter a day of real deliveries - the box a gloved driver lands one-handed is\nnot the box the label fits in. Field evidence beats parity there.\n\nStill open (needs a real photo to verify, not source reading): the Snap crop\nmaps preview-space fractions straight onto photo pixels across different\naspect ratios, and skipProcessing:true means Android may not have applied\nEXIF rotation first. Legacy Android had no crop at all.",
